SAT_CHUNK("rw/transitions/3/0",[
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.4f72648f9f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-0","passage":"<p>Many early astronomers assumed that the rings of Saturn were as old as the planet itself, roughly 4.5 billion years. Data from the Cassini spacecraft suggest otherwise: the rings are remarkably free of the dark dust that constantly rains in from space and should have darkened them over billions of years. ______ some researchers estimate that the rings may be only a few hundred million years old.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","For instance,","Accordingly,","Nevertheless,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The rings' cleanness suggests they haven't collected dust for long, so the young age estimate follows from that evidence: \"Accordingly.\" \"Nevertheless\" would signal a conclusion that goes against the evidence. \"Similarly\" and \"For instance\" don't express a conclusion drawn from evidence."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.c1524fa735","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-1","passage":"<p>The painter Georgia O'Keeffe is best known for her large, close-up images of flowers. ______ she spent decades painting the bleached bones, red hills, and adobe churches of New Mexico, and many critics consider these landscapes her most important work.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In other words","Likewise","Thus","Yet"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The first sentence gives what she's best known for, and the second says critics consider different work more important. That's a contrast: \"Yet.\" \"Thus\" implies a result, \"Likewise\" implies similarity, and \"In other words\" implies restating, and none of these fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.76263bc501","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-2","passage":"<p>Proponents of four-day workweeks argue that shorter schedules improve employee well-being without reducing output. A trial involving 61 companies in the United Kingdom offered some support for this view: most companies reported stable revenue, and employees reported less burnout. ______ the trial relied largely on self-reported measures, and companies that volunteered may have been especially well suited to the change.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Granted,","As a result,","In addition,","Specifically,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"After the supportive results, the last sentence admits limitations that weaken them. \"Granted\" introduces a concession like that. \"As a result\" wrongly treats the limitations as effects of the results. \"Specifically\" and \"In addition\" would present the limitations as more support."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.b17a54e49d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-3","passage":"<p>The Atacama Desert in Chile is among the driest places on Earth; some weather stations there have never recorded rain. ______ the desert is not lifeless. Microbes survive inside salt crusts by drawing moisture from the air, and after rare rains, fields of wildflowers bloom across the sand.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Consequently,","Indeed,","Therefore,","Even so,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Extreme dryness would suggest no life, but the text says there is life. That contrast calls for \"Even so.\" \"Consequently\" and \"Therefore\" would present the desert's life as a result of its dryness, which is illogical. \"Indeed\" would reinforce the dryness point rather than turn against it."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.4d49c3d6c4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-4","passage":"<p>Researchers wanted to know whether the arrangement of a school cafeteria affects what students eat. At several schools, they moved fruit from the end of the serving line to a spot beside the cash register, where it was displayed in colorful bowls. They made no changes to prices or menus. ______ fruit sales at those schools rose by more than 100 percent.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For example,","In contrast,","Within weeks,","Moreover,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The last sentence reports the outcome after the change, so a time-sequence transition fits: \"Within weeks.\" \"In contrast\" and \"Moreover\" misstate the relationship. \"For example\" would treat the rising sales as an illustration of the unchanged prices, which makes no sense."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.117c66ba6d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-5","passage":"<p>In the 1960s, many urban planners favored demolishing older neighborhoods to build highways and large housing projects. The writer Jane Jacobs argued that such projects destroyed the dense, mixed-use streets that made cities safe and lively. ______ she believed that sidewalks crowded with shops, homes, and pedestrians created \"eyes on the street\" that discouraged crime.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Regardless,","Specifically,","However,","Similarly,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The last sentence gives a specific reason Jacobs valued dense streets (they made cities safe), explaining her general argument in detail: \"Specifically.\" \"However\" wrongly suggests a contrast with her argument. \"Similarly\" implies a separate, parallel point. \"Regardless\" suggests she believed it despite something, which doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.cbb10691e4","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-6","passage":"<p>Most bats navigate by echolocation, emitting high-pitched calls and listening for the echoes. The large fruit bats known as flying foxes, ______ rely mainly on their keen eyesight and sense of smell to find the fruit and flowers they eat.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["as a result,","in addition,","by contrast,","for example,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Most bats echolocate, but flying foxes rely on sight and smell, which is a contrast: \"by contrast.\" \"For example\" would make flying foxes an example of echolocating bats. \"As a result\" implies causation. \"In addition\" implies an added similar point."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.ccc27853b7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-7","passage":"<p>The novelist Chinua Achebe wrote in English rather than in his first language, Igbo. Some critics argued that African writers who used colonial languages reinforced those languages' dominance. Achebe disagreed. English, he argued, could be reshaped to carry African experience and rhythms of speech. ______ his novel Things Fall Apart weaves Igbo proverbs and storytelling patterns throughout its English prose.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Instead,","Nonetheless,","Indeed,","By comparison,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The novel's use of Igbo proverbs within English puts Achebe's argument into practice, so a transition that reinforces the point fits: \"Indeed.\" \"Nonetheless\" and \"Instead\" suggest the novel contradicts or replaces his argument. \"By comparison\" suggests comparing two different things."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.749d7c47dc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-8","passage":"<p>Engineers designing the new bridge initially planned to use steel cables coated with zinc to prevent corrosion. Tests showed, however, that the salty coastal air would wear through the coating within twenty years. ______ the engineers chose cables made of a more expensive stainless alloy, which is expected to last a century.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Instead,","Still,","Likewise,","Furthermore,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The engineers replaced their original choice with a different material, so \"Instead\" fits. \"Still\" would suggest they chose something despite the test in a way that keeps the original plan. \"Likewise\" and \"Furthermore\" suggest similarity or addition, not replacement."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.78579a4ffa","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-9","passage":"<p>Economists often assume that people make purchasing decisions by carefully weighing costs and benefits. Behavioral economists have documented many exceptions. Shoppers, for instance, are more likely to buy a jar of jam when offered six flavors than when offered twenty-four. Faced with too many options, it seems, people often choose nothing at all. ______ offering consumers more choices does not always increase sales.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["On the other hand,","In other words,","For instance,","Nevertheless,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The last sentence restates the jam finding as a general principle: \"In other words.\" \"On the other hand\" signals a contrast, but the sentence agrees with the finding. \"For instance\" would introduce an example, but this is a generalization. \"Nevertheless\" suggests something unexpected given the finding."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.a866d4a555","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-10","passage":"<p>The ancient city of Pompeii is famous for having been buried by the eruption of Mount Vesuvius in 79 CE. Less well known is that the city had been badly damaged by an earthquake seventeen years earlier. ______ many buildings were still being repaired when the volcano erupted, and archaeologists have found construction materials stacked in homes and streets.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Otherwise,","Even so,","By contrast,","In fact,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The final sentence adds strong detail showing how serious the earlier damage was, reinforcing the previous sentence: \"In fact.\" \"By contrast\" and \"Even so\" signal opposition that isn't there. \"Otherwise\" means \"if not,\" which doesn't fit."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.121330693c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-11","passage":"<p>The Mediterranean diet, rich in olive oil, vegetables, and fish, has been linked to lower rates of heart disease. Some researchers have credited olive oil in particular. ______ a large study found that people who ate the diet but used little olive oil still had lower rates of heart disease than people who ate typical Western diets.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Consequently,","That is,","However,","Similarly,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The study suggests the benefit doesn't depend mainly on olive oil, which challenges the researchers' credit to it: \"However.\" \"Consequently\" and \"That is\" would present the study as following from or restating the claim. \"Similarly\" implies agreement."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.886f631b1d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-12","passage":"<p>Octopuses can change color in a fraction of a second, blending into rocks or flashing warning patterns. Remarkably, they appear to be color-blind: their eyes contain only one type of light-sensitive pigment. ______ how they match their surroundings so precisely remains a subject of active research.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","Otherwise,","Thus,","For example,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Precise color-matching by a color-blind animal is puzzling, so it follows that how they do it remains under study: \"Thus.\" \"Otherwise\" means \"if not.\" \"For example\" and \"Similarly\" don't express a conclusion."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.ef9619ad48","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-13","passage":"<p>The first vaccines against smallpox, developed in the late 1700s, used material from cowpox sores, which provided protection against the more dangerous disease. ______ the word \"vaccine\" comes from vacca, the Latin word for \"cow.\"</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["However,","Meanwhile,","In comparison,","Hence,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The word's origin follows from the use of cowpox material, so \"Hence\" fits. \"However\" suggests contrast. \"Meanwhile\" suggests something happening at the same time. \"In comparison\" suggests a comparison."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.8cef830360","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-14","passage":"<p>The Hubble Space Telescope observes mainly visible and ultraviolet light. The James Webb Space Telescope, launched in 2021, observes mainly infrared light, which can pass through clouds of dust that block visible light. ______ Webb can reveal stars forming inside dusty clouds that appear dark in Hubble's images.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["As a result,","In contrast,","For example,","Nevertheless,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Because infrared light passes through dust, Webb can see stars inside dusty clouds. The last sentence is a consequence: \"As a result.\" \"Nevertheless\" suggests something despite the previous point. \"In contrast\" wrongly suggests the sentence contrasts with Webb's abilities. \"For example\" might seem close, but the sentence states what follows from infrared observation rather than giving an example of it."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.2995f7898e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-15","passage":"<p>Some historians describe the medieval period in Europe as an age of stagnation between the achievements of ancient Rome and the Renaissance. Historian Lynn White challenged this view. He pointed to a series of medieval innovations, among them the heavy plow, the horse collar, and the mechanical clock. ______ White argued, the period laid technological foundations for later European growth.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Despite these innovations,","Before the Renaissance,","In the same way,","Far from stagnant,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"White's examples lead to the conclusion that the period was the opposite of stagnant: \"Far from stagnant.\" \"Despite these innovations\" would suggest a conclusion that contradicts them. \"In the same way\" implies a comparison. \"Before the Renaissance\" just states a time and doesn't signal his rejection of the stagnation view."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.4d62ed1672","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-16","passage":"<p>The Great Barrier Reef suffered severe coral bleaching in 2016 and 2017, when unusually warm water caused corals to expel the algae that live in their tissues. Bleached corals are not dead; if temperatures return to normal, the algae can recolonize them. ______ if high temperatures persist for weeks, the corals may starve.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["And","So","Or","But"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Recovery is possible if temperatures fall, but prolonged heat can kill corals. That's a contrast between two outcomes: \"But.\" \"So\" implies result, \"And\" implies addition, and \"Or\" implies an alternative, but the sentence contrasts the risk with the hopeful possibility."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.69dea9df5a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-17","passage":"<p>In 1911, the explorer Roald Amundsen reached the South Pole using dog sleds, while a rival British team led by Robert Falcon Scott relied partly on motor sledges and ponies. The motor sledges broke down in the cold, and the ponies struggled in deep snow. ______ Scott's team was forced to haul its own sledges for much of the journey.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["By contrast,","Previously,","Similarly,","Ultimately,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"After the sledges broke and the ponies struggled, the team ended up hauling sledges itself, the final consequence: \"Ultimately.\" \"By contrast\" and \"Similarly\" suggest comparison. \"Previously\" signals an earlier time, but the hauling came after the failures."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.086bed6d04","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-18","passage":"<p>Many people believe that goldfish have memories lasting only a few seconds. Experiments suggest otherwise. In one study, goldfish learned to push a lever for food and still remembered how to do so after three months without practice. ______ goldfish trained to respond to a particular sound continued to approach the feeding area when they heard it, even months later.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Instead,","Similarly,","Nonetheless,","In summary,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The second study provides a parallel example of long memory: \"Similarly.\" \"Instead\" and \"Nonetheless\" suggest contrast. \"In summary\" would introduce a summary, but the sentence adds a new study."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.294c1b41ee","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-19","passage":"<p>Critics sometimes dismiss graphic novels as simplified entertainment for readers who struggle with conventional books. Yet graphic novels place distinct demands on readers. ______ readers must interpret how images and words interact, infer what happens in the gaps between panels, and track visual details that may become significant pages later.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["On the whole,","As a result,","In contrast,","Among other things,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The last sentence lists some of the demands graphic novels make: \"Among other things.\" \"In contrast\" suggests opposition to the claim. \"As a result\" treats the demands as a consequence of the claim instead of details of it. \"On the whole\" signals a general summary rather than examples."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.be625b5c8a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-20","passage":"<p>For decades, sunscreen manufacturers focused mainly on blocking ultraviolet B (UVB) radiation, which causes sunburn. Research later showed that ultraviolet A (UVA) radiation, which penetrates more deeply into the skin, also contributes to skin damage and cancer. ______ regulators in many countries now require products labeled \"broad spectrum\" to protect against both types.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Instead,","In response,","Even so,","Likewise,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The regulatory requirement answers the research finding about UVA: \"In response.\" \"Likewise\" implies similarity. \"Instead\" suggests replacing UVB protection, but the rule requires both. \"Even so\" suggests the rule came despite the research."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.23352da28b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-21","passage":"<p>The Roman engineer Vitruvius wrote that buildings should have three qualities: strength, usefulness, and beauty. Modern architects still cite this formula. ______ they often disagree about how to balance the three; some prioritize function above all, while others treat a building primarily as a work of art.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Therefore,","Indeed,","For example,","Nonetheless,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"Architects accept the formula yet disagree about applying it. The disagreement is set against the shared acceptance: \"Nonetheless.\" \"Therefore\" implies the disagreement follows from citing the formula. \"For example\" and \"Indeed\" suggest support rather than tension."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.01f681a1bd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-22","passage":"<p>In 2009, the town of Brenton installed solar panels on the roofs of all its public schools. The panels were expected to supply about a third of the schools' electricity. ______ they have supplied nearly half, because the region has had sunnier weather than the models predicted.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In theory,","In practice,","In turn,","By design,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"The actual result (nearly half) is contrasted with the expectation (a third): \"In practice.\" \"In theory\" refers to expectations, which is the opposite. \"By design\" suggests the result was planned, but it came from unexpected weather. \"In turn\" suggests a chain of effects."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.9e4a25d74f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-23","passage":"<p>Wolves in Yellowstone National Park typically hunt elk, and the park's elk population fell after wolves were reintroduced in 1995. The decline had several causes, however. Drought reduced the grasses elk rely on, and human hunting outside the park increased during the same period. ______ researchers caution against attributing the entire decline to wolves.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Alternatively,","For instance,","For this reason,","In spite of this,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"Because other factors also contributed, researchers caution against blaming wolves alone. That caution is a consequence: \"For this reason.\" \"In spite of this\" suggests the caution goes against the other causes. \"For instance\" and \"Alternatively\" don't express the logical result."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.a4ac11bb95","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-24","passage":"<p>During the California Gold Rush, few miners became wealthy. Many spent their savings on the journey west and found little gold. ______ merchants who sold supplies to miners, such as Levi Strauss, who made durable work pants, often prospered.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For instance,","Meanwhile,","Similarly,","Moreover,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"While most miners struggled, merchants who supplied them were prospering during the same period. That contrast between two groups at the same time calls for \"Meanwhile.\" \"Similarly\" and \"Moreover\" would treat the merchants' success as matching or adding to the miners' failures. \"For instance\" would make the merchants an example of struggling miners."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.dc3bc318fa","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-25","passage":"<p>The mathematician Srinivasa Ramanujan had little formal training, and many of the results in his notebooks were stated without proofs. When mathematicians later worked through them, they found that most of his claims were correct. ______ some of his results turned out to be false, typically where his intuition had outrun the mathematical tools available at the time.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Accordingly,","Admittedly,","Likewise,","Specifically,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"After praising the accuracy of most claims, the text concedes some were wrong: \"Admittedly.\" \"Accordingly\" treats the errors as following from his accuracy. \"Specifically\" would introduce details of the correct claims. \"Likewise\" implies similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.c8fcfdfdcc","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-26","passage":"<p>Butterflies taste with their feet. When a female lands on a leaf, sensors on her legs detect chemicals that reveal whether the plant is a suitable food for caterpillars. ______ she lays eggs only after \"tasting\" a plant and confirming that her offspring will be able to eat it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","However,","Before this,","Thus,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The egg-laying behavior follows from her ability to test plants with her feet: \"Thus.\" \"However\" suggests contrast. \"Similarly\" suggests a parallel. \"Before this\" reverses the order of events."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.2365a07fbd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-27","passage":"<p>Early silent films were rarely silent in theaters. Live pianists or even full orchestras accompanied the screenings, and some theaters employed narrators who explained the action. ______ in Japan, such narrators, known as benshi, became celebrities in their own right, sometimes drawing larger audiences than the films themselves.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Notably,","In contrast,","Despite this,","As a result,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The last sentence highlights an especially striking case of the narrators just mentioned: \"Notably.\" \"In contrast\" and \"Despite this\" signal opposition, but the benshi were an example of the narrators, not an exception. \"As a result\" wrongly implies that live accompaniment caused the benshi's fame."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.0320171020","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data4-28","passage":"<p>Some species of trees communicate chemically. When giraffes begin browsing an acacia tree, the tree releases a gas called ethylene into the air. ______ nearby acacias that detect the gas begin producing bitter tannins in their leaves, making them less appealing to the approaching giraffes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In contrast,","Regardless,","In turn,","Similarly,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The gas triggers a response in neighboring trees, a chain of effects: \"In turn.\" \"In contrast\" and \"Regardless\" misstate the link. \"Similarly\" suggests an independent parallel rather than a response."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.f11c5260cf","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-39","passage":"<p>Historians once believed that medieval European peasants rarely traveled more than a few miles from their villages. Recent studies of marriage records, however, show that many peasants married partners from settlements twenty or thirty miles away. ______ court documents reveal that villagers regularly journeyed to distant markets and religious shrines.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Consequently,","Nevertheless,","Moreover,","By contrast,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The court documents add further evidence that peasants traveled widely, building on the marriage records: \"Moreover.\" \"Nevertheless\" and \"By contrast\" signal opposition. \"Consequently\" wrongly treats the court documents as a result of the marriage records."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.970362f1a2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-40","passage":"<p>The Japanese city of Kamikatsu aims to produce no waste that must be burned or buried. Residents sort their trash into more than forty categories. ______ the town recycles or composts about 80 percent of its waste, far more than the national average of about 20 percent.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","In contrast,","As a result,","For example,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The high recycling rate follows from residents' careful sorting: \"As a result.\" \"In contrast\" suggests opposition. \"For example\" would make the recycling rate an example of the categories. \"Similarly\" suggests a parallel."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.dde13618ef","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-41","passage":"<p>The composer Igor Stravinsky's ballet The Rite of Spring caused an uproar at its 1913 premiere in Paris; some audience members shouted and whistled so loudly that the dancers could barely hear the orchestra. ______ the work is now regarded as one of the most influential musical compositions of the twentieth century.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For this reason,","In the same way,","In other words,","Today, however,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The later acclaim contrasts with the hostile premiere. \"Today, however,\" marks both the change in time and the contrast. \"For this reason\" treats the acclaim as a result of the uproar, \"In the same way\" suggests similarity, and \"In other words\" suggests restatement."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.f9687c61e5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-42","passage":"<p>Many plants rely on bees for pollination. The corpse flower, ______ attracts carrion beetles and flies by releasing a smell resembling rotting meat.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["therefore,","for example,","likewise,","however,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The corpse flower differs from the many plants that rely on bees, so \"however\" fits. \"therefore\" suggests a result. \"for example\" would make the corpse flower an example of bee-pollinated plants. \"likewise\" suggests similarity."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.1b6c167bf6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-43","passage":"<p>In laboratory experiments, the drug slowed the growth of tumors in mice. Researchers caution that many treatments that work in mice fail in humans. ______ they plan to begin small clinical trials in human patients next year.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Therefore,","Still,","Thus,","Instead,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Despite the caution, researchers are moving ahead with trials, a concession-contrast: \"Still.\" \"Therefore\" and \"Thus\" treat the trials as a result of the caution. \"Instead\" suggests they are replacing something, but they're continuing the research."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.c9a7b95862","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-44","passage":"<p>The Inca built an extensive road network without the use of wheeled vehicles or horses. Relay runners called chasquis carried messages along these roads. ______ a message could travel as far as 240 kilometers in a single day.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In this way,","Nonetheless,","Alternatively,","In comparison,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The speed of messages resulted from the relay system just described: \"In this way.\" \"Nonetheless\" signals contrast. \"Alternatively\" suggests another option. \"In comparison\" suggests comparing two things."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.5eccc85b45","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-45","passage":"<p>Early critics of Impressionist painting complained that the artists' brushstrokes were sloppy and their scenes unfinished. The painters, ______ considered their loose technique essential to capturing fleeting effects of light and atmosphere.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["in addition,","as a result,","for instance,","for their part,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The sentence presents the painters' own view in response to the critics: \"for their part.\" \"as a result\" suggests the painters' view resulted from the complaints. \"in addition\" and \"for instance\" suggest adding or illustrating the critics' point."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.b418367488","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-46","passage":"<p>Most volcanoes form at the boundaries of tectonic plates, where plates collide or pull apart. The Hawaiian Islands, ______ lie in the middle of the Pacific Plate, far from any boundary; they formed over a hot spot of rising magma deep beneath the plate.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["as a result,","by contrast,","for example,","similarly,"],"answer":"B","explanation":"Hawaii is an exception to the pattern of volcanoes forming at plate boundaries: \"by contrast.\" \"for example\" would make Hawaii an example of boundary volcanoes. \"as a result\" suggests causation. \"similarly\" suggests the islands follow the pattern."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.c16a1747d0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-47","passage":"<p>Some economists argue that raising the minimum wage leads businesses to cut jobs. A 1994 study of fast-food restaurants in New Jersey and Pennsylvania challenged this view. ______ after New Jersey raised its minimum wage, employment at restaurants there did not fall relative to employment at restaurants in Pennsylvania, where the wage stayed the same.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Otherwise,","Likewise,","Regardless,","Specifically,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The last sentence gives the details of how the study challenged the view: \"Specifically.\" \"Regardless\" and \"Otherwise\" don't fit. \"Likewise\" suggests an additional, parallel point rather than details of the study just mentioned."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.f8e480b729","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-48","passage":"<p>The Sahara was not always a desert. Rock paintings found in the region depict giraffes, hippos, and cattle grazing in grasslands. ______ lake sediments show that between about 11,000 and 5,000 years ago, much of the Sahara received far more rain than it does today.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Instead,","However,","Additionally,","Even so,"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The lake sediments add a second kind of evidence that the Sahara was once green: \"Additionally.\" \"However,\" \"Instead,\" and \"Even so\" signal contrast, but the sediments support the paintings."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.94d5fcad98","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-49","passage":"<p>The playwright Lorraine Hansberry's A Raisin in the Sun was the first play by a Black woman to be produced on Broadway. It opened in 1959 to strong reviews. ______ the play ran for more than 500 performances and won the New York Drama Critics' Circle Award.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Ultimately,","Previously,","For example,","Conversely,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The long run and the award came after the strong opening: \"Ultimately.\" \"Conversely\" suggests opposition. \"For example\" would make the run an example of the reviews. \"Previously\" places the events before the opening, which is illogical."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.df45299af9","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-50","passage":"<p>Humans can distinguish about one million colors. Mantis shrimp have up to twelve types of color receptors, compared with humans' three. ______ researchers were surprised to find that mantis shrimp are actually worse than humans at telling similar colors apart.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Nevertheless,","Consequently,","Furthermore,","In other words,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"With so many color receptors, one would expect better color discrimination, so the finding is surprising given what came before: \"Nevertheless.\" \"Consequently\" suggests the poorer ability follows from the extra receptors. \"Furthermore\" and \"In other words\" suggest addition or restatement."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.1fc22feea7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-51","passage":"<p>Many early automobiles ran on electricity rather than gasoline; in 1900, about a third of cars in the United States were electric. Electric cars were quiet and easy to start, ______ they could travel only short distances before their batteries needed recharging.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["but","for","and","so"],"answer":"A","explanation":"The limited range contrasts with the advantages just listed: \"but.\" \"so\" and \"for\" suggest cause and effect, and \"and\" suggests addition."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.27df8e7e9c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-52","passage":"<p>The Great Pacific Garbage Patch is often imagined as a floating island of trash. In reality, most of its debris consists of tiny plastic fragments, many smaller than a grain of rice, scattered through the upper layers of the water. ______ the patch cannot be seen in satellite images and is difficult to clean up with nets.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For this reason,","In contrast,","For instance,","Even so,"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Because the debris is tiny and scattered, it can't be seen from space and is hard to net: \"For this reason.\" \"Even so\" and \"In contrast\" suggest opposition. \"For instance\" suggests an example rather than a consequence."},
{"id":"g.rw.transitions.3.1af09161e6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"transitions","difficulty":3,"group":"hard-hard_data6-53","passage":"<p>The Greenland shark grows about one centimeter per year. Because adults can reach lengths of more than five meters, scientists long suspected the species was extremely long-lived, but they had no way to measure the sharks' ages directly. ______ in 2016, researchers used radiocarbon dating on proteins in the sharks' eyes and estimated that one shark was about 400 years old.</p>","prompt":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For example,","Otherwise,","Similarly,","Then,"],"answer":"D","explanation":"The 2016 study came after the long period without a way to measure ages, finally providing one: \"Then.\" \"Otherwise\" means \"if not.\" \"For example\" would make the study an example of the lack of methods. \"Similarly\" suggests a parallel."}
]);
